    "body": "Derive include descriptions from the including source or include search root. This avoids build directory paths in generated code. Honor explicit logical names for sources inside the working directory as well.\r\n\r\nOnly the source file name that ends up in a built extension module is changed here; paths for file access and diagnostics are kept the same.\r\n\r\nDiffoscope output comparing strings in an extension module in SciPy from two wheel builds with different build-directory depths:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n-../scipy/cluster/hierarchy/_structures.pxi\r\n+../../../scipy/cluster/hierarchy/_structures.pxi\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter this change, both now use `scipy/cluster/hierarchy/_structures.pxi`.\r\n\r\n***\r\n\r\nAI coding tool usage declaration: I used Codex with GPT 6 to review this locally and ensure the fix is complete (I had missed the Scanning.py change, it proposed a change there that I had to whittle down to a minimal diff). \r\n\r\nChange validated in a scipy-release CI job. Integration test for the whole set of reproducibility fixes coming as a follow-up, as discussed in gh-7982. ",
    "closed_at": null,
